-- title:
--   G Hat Pair Product Sdd Op Rel Triple
-- statement:
--   **A pair-product relation lifts unchanged to a triple question space.**
--
--   Let $(m,q,d)$ have a field model, let $\psi_{AB}$ be a bipartite quantum state, let $F$ be a slice-indexed polynomial family, let $\gamma,\zeta$ be error parameters, and let $r\in\mathbb N$. Suppose the two completed-slice pair-product families are related under the uniform distribution on pairs of slice questions with
--
--   $$
--   E_{\mathrm{pair}}=138m\left(\gamma^{1/16}+\zeta^{1/16}+(d/q)^{1/16}\right).
--   $$
--
--   If $P_L(x_1,x_2)$ and $P_R(x_1,x_2)$ denote those two pair-product families, then the same families, ignoring an independent tail point tuple, satisfy
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi_{AB},\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathcal Q\times\mathcal Q\times\mathbb{F}_q^r)}
--   \left((x_1,x_2,\mathbf y)\mapsto P_L(x_1,x_2),
--   (x_1,x_2,\mathbf y)\mapsto P_R(x_1,x_2);E_{\mathrm{pair}}\right).
--   $$
--
--   The result supplies the triple-question relation used by the commutation move step.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.gHatPairProduct_sddOpRel_triple`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
